# Model weights. This is the PUBLIC repo: it has never tracked a single model
# blob (0 in all of history) and CI builds without them ("Build (no model
# blobs)"); operators download them at first run. The private repo LFS-tracks
# these same files — do NOT copy this ignore there.
#
# Without these lines the weights sit untracked-AND-unignored, so one `git add
# -A` stages ~2.6 GB into public history through the *.onnx LFS filter in
# .gitattributes. That is not hypothetical: the same move already leaked the
# orchestration skills (agent-postmortems.md §30, accepted-tracked-skills-no-removal).
*.onnx
*.gguf
*onnx_data
*.int8-backup
*.fp32-backup

# OnnxSessionCache artifacts (generated at runtime, machine-specific)
*.onnx.optimized
*.onnx.opt-meta
*.onnx.sha256
# CUDA-EP variant caches (tempdoc 402 follow-up; patterns above don't match
# *.onnx.cuda.optimized — the .cuda. infix shifts the suffix)
*.cuda.optimized
*.cuda.opt-meta
